   "notes": "Machine-typed (born-digital-looking, scanned) tables, Gary Ott, Recorder, 2012. THE PAGE CONTRADICTS ITSELF AND IS TRANSCRIBED FROM THE FORM: the page is titled 'Itemized Contributions Received' but the filer pasted the EXPENDITURE table template underneath it, so its column headers read 'Date Expended | Recipent Name | Purpose | Amount | In-Kind?' and its grand-total row is labelled 'TOTAL EXPENDITURES MADE'. The rows themselves are money coming IN (two Key Bank fee refunds and ten Gary Ott deposits) and the page total 180.00 equals the Summary Page's stated CONTRIBUTIONS figure, not its expenditures figure (106.11). So this is the contributions side; the header wording is the filer's template error. Because the pasted template has a Purpose column and NO address or occupation column, donor_city/donor_state are blank by non-existence. The account is essentially dormant: the expenditures side is 24 Key Bank fee lines and the contributions side is two fee refunds plus ten small deposits by the candidate himself. Both tables print an In-Kind? column that is EMPTY on every row. One expenditure date is printed 03/08/13 sitting between 02/17/12 and 03/08/12 - a well-formed filer typo, kept verbatim per contract. FIELD-SHIFT SCREEN: machine-set columns; 12 dates / 12 names / 12 purposes / 12 amounts on p3 and 24/24/24/24 on p4; both pages gate exactly. No shift found."
